@ifnottex
@node Top
@top agent: AI coding agent integration for Emacs

This manual describes the features and customization options for the Emacs Lisp package @samp{agent.el}.

When you start a Claude or Codex session from a registered Elpaca build tree@comma{}
Agent uses that package’s source checkout. Elpaca can replace build directories
during a rebuild@comma{} which invalidates a running process’s working directory. This
applies to explicit session directories and directories inferred from the current
buffer. Other directories retain their usual behavior. A missing registered source
directory prevents the session from starting.

@end ifnottex

