@node Overview
@chapter Overview

@samp{agent.el} collects the Emacs integration layer for AI coding command-line tools. It provides a shared session model@comma{} a unified transient menu@comma{} notification handling@comma{} terminal helpers@comma{} backend modules for Claude Code and Codex@comma{} and an optional chief-of-staff loop.

The package is split into a small backend-agnostic core and focused modules:

@multitable {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa} {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa}
@headitem Module
@tab Role
@item @samp{agent.el}
@tab Core: backend registry@comma{} session identity and state machine@comma{} session keys and teardown@comma{} unified orchestration commands (handoff@comma{} restart@comma{} exit@comma{} resume@comma{} branch navigation@comma{} skills@comma{} backtrace debugging)@comma{} transient menu@comma{} alerts@comma{} theme sync
@item @samp{agent-account.el}
@tab Multi-account support shared by all backends: selection@comma{} persistence@comma{} per-account config homes@comma{} symlinked shared state
@item @samp{agent-usage.el}
@tab Per-account usage store and poller shared by all backends
@item @samp{agent-doom-modeline.el}
@tab Optional @samp{doom-modeline} integration: the @samp{ai-session} modeline of session buffers@comma{} defined only once @samp{doom-modeline} is loaded
@item @samp{agent-capture.el}
@tab Persisted Org prompt capture@comma{} keyed to the session it targets
@item @samp{agent-project.el}
@tab Account-scoped project sources: registry and path-pattern candidates@comma{} model ranking@comma{} and the project prompt for things that carry no directory of their own
@item @samp{agent-slack.el}
@tab Slack-message-to-project routing: reads the message at point as text with no directory of its own@comma{} leaving the project to the shared project reader
@item @samp{agent-forge.el}
@tab Forge-notification-to-project routing: starts a session in the working tree of the repository the notification belongs to
@item @samp{agent-mu4e.el}
@tab Email-to-project routing: reads the mu4e message at point as a maildir path@comma{} leaving the project to the shared project reader
@item @samp{agent-org-linear.el}
@tab Linear-issue-to-project routing: routes an issue @samp{org-linear} mirrors as the org TODO it is@comma{} ranking projects by its Linear project and adding its URL to the prompt
@item @samp{agent-snippet.el}
@tab Yasnippet TAB expansion and snippet insertion in eat-based session buffers
@item @samp{agent-todo.el}
@tab Org TODO workflow that works with any backend: routing the entry at point to a session
@item @samp{agent-util.el}
@tab File helpers shared by the backends@comma{} such as reading a transcript's first line whatever its length; depends on no other module
@item @samp{agent-claude.el}
@tab Claude Code backend: integrates @samp{claude-code.el} with status and usage polling@comma{} hook setup@comma{} and @code{agent-claude-mode}
@item @samp{agent-claude-cli.el}
@tab Quarantined undocumented Claude CLI conventions: Keychain credential naming@comma{} the usage API endpoint@comma{} the @samp{~/.claude/projects/} directory encoding@comma{} transcript JSONL parsing@comma{} and the @samp{.claude.json} merge engine
@item @samp{agent-codex.el}
@tab Codex backend: integrates @samp{codex.el} with theme sync@comma{} @samp{codex exec} execution@comma{} @samp{config.toml} helpers@comma{} modeline helpers@comma{} and @code{agent-codex-mode}
@item @samp{agent-chief.el}
@tab Inspectable chief-of-staff loop: Emacs owns timers@comma{} state@comma{} context collection@comma{} and notifications@comma{} while Claude Code or Codex provides one-shot judgment on each tick
@item @samp{agent-setup.el}
@tab First-run checks: finds the agent CLIs and @samp{emacsclient}@comma{} starts the Emacs server@comma{} checks the hooks passed to Claude sessions and offers to remove copies left in global settings@comma{} offers to link the bundled skills@comma{} and reports what is left
@end multitable

The main workflow is to load @samp{agent.el}@comma{} require the backend modules you use@comma{} and enable their minor modes (see @ref{Backend minor modes, , Backend minor modes}); loading a backend module installs nothing by itself. Once the Claude and Codex modules are active@comma{} @samp{M-x agent-menu} and @samp{M-x agent-select-session} operate across both tools. Sessions are listed with their account in a column of its own@comma{} highlighted when waiting for input@comma{} and disambiguated by project and instance name when several sessions share a directory.

The package depends on @samp{transient} for menus@comma{} @samp{consult} for completion@comma{} @samp{claude-code.el} for the Claude backend@comma{} and @samp{codex.el} for the Codex backend. All four are declared in the package metadata so that the package manager builds @samp{agent} with them available; the backend modules hard-require their respective backend at load time. Optional integrations use packages such as @samp{yasnippet}@comma{} @samp{doom-modeline}@comma{} @samp{gptel}@comma{} @samp{agent-log}@comma{} and @samp{monet} when those are available.

