The command @code{agent-chief-start-session} starts or reuses a dedicated Claude Code or Codex session using @code{agent-chief-session-instance-name}@comma{} sends the chief-of-staff operating contract into the session@comma{} asks the model to request today's plan there@comma{} and starts the heartbeat timer. The command @code{agent-chief-switch-to-session} jumps back to that session so the user can reply normally.

The command @code{agent-chief-start} starts only the repeating Emacs timer. Without a prefix argument it also schedules an immediate tick; with a prefix argument@comma{} it waits @code{agent-chief-interval} seconds before the first tick. @code{agent-chief-stop} cancels the timer. @code{agent-chief-tick} runs one check using @code{agent-chief-mode}. @code{agent-chief-session-heartbeat} forces a session-mode heartbeat@comma{} while @code{agent-chief-stateless-tick} forces one stateless JSON-decision check.

The command @code{agent-chief-open-state} opens the auditable Org state file. @code{agent-chief-add-note} appends a manual note@comma{} and @code{agent-chief-set-day-plan} appends today's plan. When a chief session is active@comma{} both commands also submit the new context into that session. These commands are intentionally simple: the durable source of truth remains ordinary text that can be reviewed@comma{} edited@comma{} and audited outside the model.

