The Claude commands expose workflows that are specific to Claude Code; handoff@comma{} restart@comma{} exit@comma{} resume@comma{} branch navigation@comma{} skill execution@comma{} backtrace debugging@comma{} TODO workflows@comma{} and Slack-message routing use the unified @code{agent-*} commands described above. @code{agent-claude-start-or-switch} starts Claude under the selected account or opens the unified switcher. @code{agent-claude-select-account} persists an account choice@comma{} and @code{agent-claude-init-account} prepares a new account directory with shared configuration files and symlinks.

The branch and TODO commands that used to be Claude's own are now the shared @code{agent-create-branch}@comma{} @code{agent-switch-branch}@comma{} and @code{agent-send-todo-at-point}; @code{agent-claude-create-branch}@comma{} @code{agent-claude-switch-branch}@comma{} and @code{agent-claude-send-todo-at-point} remain as obsolete aliases.

@code{agent-claude-start-status-polling} and @code{agent-claude-stop-status-polling} start and stop status polling for the current Claude buffer by hand. Polling is started and stopped for you with the session@comma{} so these are maintenance commands rather than part of a normal workflow; they are available through @samp{M-x} and are not in @code{agent-menu}.

The setup command @code{agent-claude-setup-config} ensures that Claude's statusline@comma{} Stop hook@comma{} Notification hook@comma{} and turn-lifecycle hooks are present in @samp{~/.claude/settings.json}@comma{} for sessions started outside Emacs; sessions this package starts receive them through @samp{--settings} without it. @code{agent-claude-remove-global-config} removes them again. @code{agent-claude-ensure-state-hook-config} installs only the turn-lifecycle hooks listed in @code{agent-claude--state-hook-events}. The backend does not run setup automatically when loaded; run the setup command explicitly when installing or repairing hook configuration.

